  "notes": "⛔ **The only major-mode entry in this batch, and that is the whole model.** The research calls it \"the most consonant harmony in this section\" — `Imaj7–IV` and `ii–V` soul cycles built on a Midnight Star sample rather than a minor funk vamp — so `session.scales` is major-weighted, `session.keys` are the bare major spellings the dataset already uses for its major lanes, and the progression families are upper-case degrees. Everything else follows from supporting a sung lead: `chordToneBias` 0.82 and `halfStepDissonance` 0.03 are the most consonant numbers here, `intervals.leap` is the lowest at 0.06, the contour is arch-first rather than riff-first because a sung R&B line arcs, and the kit is deliberately low-intensity (kick on 1 and the and-of-3, light swing). The bass is \"smooth… round, sustained, melodic, sitting well forward\", so `glideProb` 0.42 with major-mode passing tones rather than the blues set the rest of this batch uses. ⚠ `medium` on the research's high-medium; the INFERRED parameter is the exact cycle — \"`Imaj7–IV`/`ii–V` soul cycles\" is a family name, not a documented progression, so the four authored families are the standard soul set inside that description. ⚠ The wah-wah guitar the research names as the counter-line has no timbre of its own; the counter is authored as density and style only.",
